# Pf39c2-social-pilot-03 T09 (`social/Dockerfile`).
#
# This is the .dockerignore Docker ACTUALLY reads for `social/Dockerfile`'s
# build: `docker build -f social/Dockerfile .` uses this repo root as its
# build context (required — `social/Dockerfile` needs `content/output/` and
# `content/social/`, which sit outside `social/`, see `social/DOCKER.md`),
# and Docker resolves `.dockerignore` relative to the CONTEXT root, not the
# Dockerfile's own directory. `social/.dockerignore` also exists (this
# task's own file list asked for it) but is not the file Docker consults for
# that build command — see its header comment. Keep the `social/`-scoped
# patterns below in sync with it by hand.
#
# If this repo ever grows a second Dockerfile (e.g. for `web/`), broaden
# this file rather than assuming these patterns are social-pilot-specific.

# Never send the whole monorepo's dependency trees into any image's build
# context — every Dockerfile installs its own fresh, platform-matched
# node_modules instead (see social/Dockerfile's ffmpeg-static/playwright
# comments on why a host-built node_modules would be wrong to copy in).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

.git/
.vercel/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Social pilot render output and per-day job logs/stray pending-flip state
# from local runs — never something a build should bake in as if it were
# committed data. content/social/*.json schedules and render-exclusions.json
# themselves are NOT excluded here — job.ts/cli.ts read those at runtime.
social/out/
content/social/job-logs/

# Pipeline intermediates/fixtures/source texts and the web app — irrelevant
# to the social image, and content/pipeline/ in particular can be large.
content/pipeline/
content/fixtures/
content/source/
web/
functions/

# Editor/OS noise and secrets.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.log
test-results/
